# 0.8.18 Slice 5 — #5 vector-equivalence probe (shipped surface)

> **Status: IMPLEMENTED (RED/GREEN TDD).** Schema-migration slice (18→19) →
> **HITL-gated landing**. Authority: `dev/design/0.8.18-slice-0-vector-equivalence-publish-design.md`
> §U1 (R-VEQ-1..R-VEQ-6) + `dev/adr/ADR-0.8.18-vector-equivalence-self-check.md`
> (ACCEPTED / HITL-SIGNED 2026-07-09). This note documents the SHIPPED surface;
> the requirements + RED-testable ACs live in the Slice-0 design package.
>
> **Requirement traceability (added 2026-07-28, Steward — bookkeeping, no design change):** design of
> record for **`R-20-VC` / TC-68** (0.8.20 Slice 22) — cache this probe against an embedder-identity
> fingerprint so `Engine::open` cost is constant again, **preserving** the guarantee rather than
> weakening it. Back-linked per TC-92.

## What it is

An open-time self-check that re-embeds the 45 committed equivalence probes
(`fathomdb-embedder/tests/fixtures/candle_onnx_equivalence_probes.txt`, copied
crate-local as `fathomdb-engine/src/vector_equivalence_probes.txt` with a
byte-identity drift-guard test) with the LIVE backend and refuses dense retrieval
if the backend has diverged beyond the frozen D4 floor. It is **ADDITIVE** to the
existing cross-vendor `EmbedderIdentity` refusal (`check_embedder_profile`) — the
identity gate proves the backend *claims* the same embedder; the probe proves it
*produces equivalent 1-bit codes* (R-VEQ-5, additive-only).

## The FROZEN D4 tolerance floor

- **P1 (Phase-1 binary):** mean-centered `embedding_bin` sign-flip count floor =
  **0 (exact)** — any single flip across the 45 probes ⇒ divergence
  (`VECTOR_EQUIVALENCE_P1_FLIP_FLOOR = 0`).
- **P2 (Phase-2 float):** un-centered L2 ε = **1e-5** — `‖reembed − reference‖₂`
  (`vec_distance_l2` semantics) `> 1e-5` ⇒ divergence
  (`VECTOR_EQUIVALENCE_L2_EPSILON = 1e-5`). Single named const; final ε gets a
  HITL look at landing.

BOTH are asserted (correctness trap: asserting only P1 lets P2 float drift
silently within recalled candidates; asserting only P2 lets a centered-code flip
silently drop candidates from Phase-1 recall).

## Storage (R-VEQ-1) — schema step 19 (`SCHEMA_VERSION` 18→19)

New internal table `_fathomdb_embed_probe(probe_ordinal, probe_text,
reference_vec BLOB, embedder_name, embedder_revision, dim)`. Stores **UN-centered
f32 references ONLY** — the P1 bits are **NEVER persisted** (recomputed at check
time from the un-centered reference + the live pinned `mean_vec`, U1-d). The 45
rows are written by the engine at OPEN, at the first open where a vector kind
already exists (after mean-recovery + `ensure_vector_partition`) — this covers the
v18→v19 upgrade case and a kind registered in a prior session (fix-1 DEFECT #4, see
below); the migration creates the empty table only. Pure additive `CREATE TABLE`
(eu7 no-op basis — no vec0 rewrite).

## Check (R-VEQ-2/3) — where + how

`run_vector_equivalence_probe` runs in `Engine::open_with_migrations` on the
FINAL post-recovery writer connection (**after** open-time mean-recovery/requantize
and `ensure_vector_partition`, so it reads the FINAL live `mean_vec` — U1-b).
First registration persists references (dense stays enabled). A subsequent open
re-embeds each probe and asserts:

- **P1:** `vec_quantize_binary(sign(x − mean_vec))` bits for reference vs reembed,
  via the SAME SQL `vec_quantize_binary` path as `build_vector_phase1_sql`; the
  Hamming (flip) count must be `≤ 0`.
- **P2:** un-centered L2 must be `≤ 1e-5`.

Mean-centering is gated by `identity_requires_mean_centering(identity)` ∧
`mean_vec` pinned (true only for the default `fathomdb-bge-small-en-v1.5`;
NoopEmbedder no-op), applied symmetrically to both sides with an un-centered
fallback (R-VEQ-3c).

### Fail-SAFE, never fail-open (fix-1 DEFECT #1)

Any inability to RUN or VERIFY the probe ⇒ `dense_disabled = true` + a clear
reason (refuse the un-verifiable dense/fused arm; the text-only/FTS path still
serves). `Engine::open` still SUCCEEDS (never wedges on a panicking caller
embedder), but it never serves dense on an arm it could not verify — same-identity
backend drift on an un-verifiable arm is exactly what #5 exists to catch (R-VEQ-4
"loud typed refuse, never silent"). Concretely:

- **CHECK path:** a probe embed that panics / errors / returns wrong-dim, a
  malformed or missing reference row, an unreadable pinned `mean_vec`, or a
  `vec_quantize_binary` / L2 SQL failure ⇒ cannot verify ⇒ `dense_disabled = true`
  (never skip-and-serve).
- **POPULATION path (first registration):** if the embedder cannot produce EVERY
  reference vector (panic / error), no baseline can be established ⇒
  `dense_disabled = true`. References are written in ONE transaction, so a partial
  set is never persisted (a later open cleanly retries population).

The distinct-identity cross-vendor `EmbedderIdentity` refusal
(`check_embedder_profile`) stays the PRIMARY gate and #5 is ADDITIVE-ONLY
(R-VEQ-5) — but on the vector arm #5 fails CLOSED, not open.

### Baseline establishment: OPEN-time, identity-gated (fix-1 DEFECT #4)

The baseline is established at OPEN, at the first open where a vector kind already
exists (the population path in `run_vector_equivalence_probe`). This covers both
holes DEFECT #4 raised:

- **(b) v18→v19 upgrade with pre-existing vector kinds:** the baseline is
  established at the first v19 open (the migration only CREATEs the empty table),
  captured from the **identity-matched** embedder — the same open already runs
  `check_embedder_profile`, which refuses a different-*identity* backend — so the
  baseline is the same *claimed* embedder and future backend drift is caught. If
  the embedder cannot be run at that open ⇒ `dense_disabled = true` (fail-SAFE,
  DEFECT #1).
- **(a) a vector kind registered POST-OPEN (prior session):** the baseline is
  captured at the NEXT open (same gate + population), again identity-gated. Serving
  vector queries in the REGISTERING session is safe regardless: the serving backend
  IS the backend that built those vectors, so there is nothing to diverge from
  in-session; the probe exists to catch *cross-open* drift, which is caught from
  the next-open baseline onward.

**Deliberate deviation from the literal "store at registration" (write-path),
justified + flagged.** The baseline is NOT captured in the registering session's
write path. A write must **never block on the embedder** — that is the entire
basis of async projection, pinned by
`ac_029_canonical_writes_complete_under_projection_stall`, the PR-9 embed watchdog,
and the PR-9 abandoned-thread-leak bounds. Running 45 synchronous probe embeds at
the registration point would violate all three (and hang/degrade under a stalling
or hanging embedder). In-session serving is already safe (same backend), so the
only thing write-path establishment would add is capturing *this* session's backend
rather than the next open's — a marginal gain at the cost of breaking a load-bearing
invariant. It is therefore done at open instead.

**Residual (accepted, identical for both (a) and (b)):** a same-*identity* backend
that drifted BEFORE the baseline-establishing open (the pre-existing/prior-session
vectors were built by it and become the baseline) is not retroactively caught. This
is acceptable because #5 is additive-only (R-VEQ-5) and U3 measured same-identity
candle CPU↔CUDA at 0 / 17280 flips; the guard is "baseline-now + catch-future-drift",
not a retroactive audit of already-persisted vectors.

## Refusal (R-VEQ-4) — degraded-open + single choke point

On divergence the open **SUCCEEDS** with `dense_disabled = true` (NOT an open
error). The query-time refusal is a new **`EngineError::VectorEquivalenceMismatch
{ reason }`** raised at the SINGLE choke point `Engine::search_inner_with_stats`,
BEFORE any embedding / vector SQL / graph seeding / CE rerank — covering EVERY
vector-dependent arm (`search`, `search_filtered`, `search_reranked`,
`search_explained`, `search_expand`, and the `use_graph_arm` graph arm, which all
funnel through it). Bindings map it to leaf classes/codes at parity with
`EmbedderIdentityMismatch`:

- Rust: `EngineError::VectorEquivalenceMismatch { reason }` (`stable_code =
  "VectorEquivalenceMismatchError"`).
- Python: `fathomdb.errors.VectorEquivalenceMismatchError` (leaf of `EngineError`;
  carries `reason`).
- TypeScript: `VectorEquivalenceMismatchError` (leaf of `FathomDbError`; carries
  `reason`); envelope code `FDB_VECTOR_EQUIVALENCE_MISMATCH`.

### FTS-only escape hatch

`Engine::search_text_only(query)` (+ Py `search_text_only`, TS `searchTextOnly`)
is the explicit text-only / FTS-only path. It does NOT embed the query and does
NOT route through the choke point, so it NEVER raises the refusal — FTS stays
serviceable in degraded mode (D2 / codex R2 U1-2). It is a governed application
command (added to `src/conformance/governed-surface-allowlist.json`).

## Observability (R-VEQ-6)

`OpenReport.dense_disabled` (+ `dense_disabled_reason`) surfaced on Rust / Python
/ TypeScript. Engine accessors `dense_disabled()`, `dense_disabled_reason()`, and
the telemetry counter `vector_equivalence_refusal_count()` (increments per
refused query) — all observability, excluded from the governed-command allowlist.
The state is RE-DERIVED at every open (the probe re-runs), so a reopen with a
still-divergent backend stays degraded (never silently re-enables dense) and a
reopen with a matching backend clears it.

## Tests

- Engine (Rust, shipped behaviour): `fathomdb-engine/tests/vector_equivalence_probe.rs`
  (persistence, two-sided divergent-trips / noise-does-not, P1 exact-flip-count,
  P2-only, centering gate, degraded-open, every-arm-refuses, FTS-serviceable,
  report + counter + reopen-sticky) and `..._fixture_drift.rs` (drift guard).
  **fix-1 additions:** `panicking_embedder_at_check_fails_safe_not_open`,
  `erroring_embedder_at_check_fails_safe_not_open`,
  `population_failure_fails_safe_and_persists_no_partial_baseline` (DEFECT #1
  fail-SAFE); `post_open_registration_serves_in_session_and_baselines_at_next_open`
  (DEFECT #4 hole (a) — safe in-session serving + next-open identity-gated baseline
  - forward-drift caught);
  `mc_required_with_pin_same_backend_does_not_trip`,
  `mc_required_with_pin_centered_flip_trips_dense`,
  `mc_reflect_without_pin_takes_uncentered_path_zero_flips` (DEFECT #5 / CONCERN #9,
  the production MC-required-with-pin P1 branch — the last two contrast the SAME
  reflect backend with vs without a pinned mean, proving centering is applied);
  `upgrade_from_v18_with_kind_and_pinned_mean_establishes_baseline_and_checks`
  (CONCERN #6, genuine v18→v19 upgrade).
- Schema (Rust): `fathomdb-schema/tests/step19_migration.rs`.
- SDK surface parity (X1, verified on the MAIN compiled module):
  `src/python/tests/test_vector_equivalence_probe.py`,
  `src/ts/tests/vector-equivalence-probe.test.ts`, plus the governed-surface
  suites (`test_surface.py` / `surface.test.ts`) — now including an explicit
  `search_text_only` / `searchTextOnly` live-presence guard (fix-1 CONCERN #7).

## Landing

Schema bump (18→19) ⇒ **HITL-gated landing** regardless of the standing mandate.

