commit 980a757a0bd56ff808e806b6169eed11c5d70f4c
Author: Corey Thompson <coreyt@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 28 17:45:32 2026 -0500

    fix(TC-76/#99): GREEN — one vec0-delete primitive that neutralizes long metadata
    
    `delete_vector_partition_row` is now THE way this crate deletes a
    `vector_default` row by rowid. It blanks the `attr_<hex>` columns first, then
    deletes. vec0's UPDATE path takes the `n <= 12 && prev_n > 12` branch
    (sqlite-vec.c:8300-8319), which deletes the `_metadatatext<NN>` shadow row AND
    returns SQLITE_OK, so the following DELETE has no over-length value left to
    clear and never reaches the defective `vec0Update_Delete_ClearMetadata` branch.
    Measured: the `embedding` bytes and the other metadata columns survive the
    metadata-only UPDATE verbatim, and the shadow row is gone — erasure-COMPLETE,
    not merely error-suppressing.
    
    All six by-rowid vec0 delete sites now route through it:
      - `prune_edge_projection_shadows` (edge re-projection)
      - `run_pin_and_requantize_pass` (mean-vec pin DELETE+INSERT; attr values are
        read BEFORE the delete and re-bound after, so neutralizing cannot lose them)
      - the open-path orphan sweep
      - the two edge-supersession prunes (G0 logical_id, G11 triple)
      - the row-owned projection registry, via `delete_row_owned_projection`
    `truncate_row_projections_in` gets the same treatment table-wide: an unqualified
    `DELETE FROM vector_default` still dispatches vec0's per-row delete and so fails
    on the first over-length row.
    
    No-op when no `filterable` projection is declared (`actual_vector_attr_columns`
    empty) — every pre-Slice-15e corpus issues exactly the statements it always did.
    
    The bare-vec0 test in tests/tc76_vec0_long_metadata_delete.rs is the tripwire:
    it fails when sqlite-vec ships a fix for #99, which is the signal to delete the
    neutralize step. SCHEMA_VERSION untouched (24); no migration.
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013RjME68BUnxzySCxgGU79v

