commit 423e5f227ea171da081ad0127dbf46d16e46c108
Author: Corey Thompson <coreyt@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 28 18:59:49 2026 -0500

    fix(TC-67): GREEN — the excluded kinds are REPORTED, by kind, on the delta
    
    0.8.20 Slice 22 (R-20-VC), leg 1. Populates
    `ProjectionDelta.vector_unsupported_kinds` — the additive field landed at RED —
    with the vector-eligible node kinds the vector writer can never commit.
    
    THREE FUNCTIONS, ONE SCAN.
    
      * `vector_eligible_node_kinds(tx)` — extracted from
        `enqueue_declared_vector_backfill`. `SELECT DISTINCT kind FROM
        canonical_nodes WHERE row_kind IN ('leaf','coverage') ORDER BY kind`, i.e.
        the `index_targets_for_row_kind` vector-eligibility predicate. `graph` rows
        stay excluded on a ROW-KIND axis that has nothing to do with the `kind`
        vocabulary — reporting them would be a different, false statement.
        `DISTINCT … ORDER BY` yields the sorted, de-duplicated ordering for free.
    
      * `unsupported_vector_kinds(tx)` — the COMPLEMENT of what enrolment takes:
        the same list, filtered by `!kind_is_vector_committable`. Enrolment and the
        report therefore partition ONE list. Two hand-copied queries would be the
        TC-56 drift shape, and here the drift would be silent in the worst
        direction: a report describing a different set from the one actually
        excluded.
    
      * `apply_projection_config` — assigns the report when `vector_declared_after`,
        i.e. scoped to a live dense-arm declaration (no `searchable→vector`
        projection ⇒ nothing to be unsupported FOR ⇒ no noise on `filterable`/FTS
        -only calls), but OUTSIDE the `dense_arm_live` branch beneath it.
    
    THE ONE PLACEMENT DECISION, stated: the report is NOT gated on a live embedder.
    The enrolment it mirrors is (Q6a graceful-absent), but `resolve_source_type`'s
    vocabulary is a compile-time constant, so "this kind can never be embedded" is
    equally true in a no-embedder session. Gating it would hide the PERMANENT fact
    behind the TRANSIENT one — the exact conflation TC-67 exists to end, and a
    graceful-absent caller is precisely the caller who needs to know that attaching
    an embedder later still will not embed these kinds.
    
    It is assigned AFTER `delta.unchanged` is computed and does NOT feed it: a STATE
    report, not a diff. An idempotent re-apply carries it with `unchanged = true`,
    which is also the documented refresh path for the declare-time residual.
    
    WHAT DID NOT CHANGE, deliberately:
      * `resolve_source_type`'s vocabulary — NOT grown (HITL option (c));
      * the Pack-1 D3 partition-key lock — NOT touched;
      * readiness — an un-enrolled kind is still not outstanding work, so
        `dense_readiness` still reads `ready`; pinned by
        `readiness_semantics_are_unchanged_by_the_report`;
      * enrolment itself — the reported kinds are still un-enrolled, still carry no
        vector, still produce no `projection_failures` row. TC-67 changes what the
        engine SAYS, not what it does.
    
    GREEN: `cargo test -p fathomdb-engine --test
    tc67_unsupported_vector_kind_report` = 7 passed / 0 failed (was 1/6 at 34b13c61).
    
    No regression in the suites that own this code path:
      slice15d_projection_registry 24/24 · slice20_dense_readiness 8/8 ·
      slice20c_flush_barrier 12/12 · slice21c_vector_role_gate 5/5 ·
      projection_runtime 12/12 (1 ignored, pre-existing).
    
    `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets` = 0, zero warnings.
    Governed-surface pin rc=0, allowlist sha 555e6ae7… unchanged.
    `SCHEMA_VERSION` still 24 — no migration step.
    
    Refs: dev/plans/plan-0.8.20.md §3 R-20-VC (TC-67).
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013RjME68BUnxzySCxgGU79v

