 14818	/// `rc` to `SQLITE_OK`. `vec0Update_Delete` (`sqlite-vec.c:9027`) reads
 14819	/// `101 != SQLITE_OK` as a failure and aborts the entire `DELETE`. The
 14820	/// INSERT/UPDATE twin of that code (`sqlite-vec.c:8258-8320`) is saved by an
 14821	/// unconditional `rc = sqlite3_blob_close(...)` after its switch, which is why
 14822	/// only DELETE carries the defect — and why the neutralizing `UPDATE` below is a
 14823	/// sound workaround rather than the same bug by another name.
 14824	///
 14825	/// # Why FathomDB is exposed
 14826	///
 14827	/// `vector_default` carries three plain-TEXT metadata columns
 14828	/// ([`vector_partition_create_sql`]): `kind`, `status` and one `attr_<hex>` per
 14829	/// declared `filterable` projection. Only the `attr_*` VALUES are caller-supplied
 14830	/// and unbounded, and Slice 15e stores them marker-encoded (`\x01 || V`), so a
 14831	/// raw attribute value of **12 or more UTF-8 bytes** trips #99 and makes
 14832	/// `erase_source` / `purge` / edge supersession / the open-path orphan sweep fail
 14833	/// with [`EngineError::Storage`], leaving the row AND its shadowed value at rest.
 14834	/// `kind` is bounded to `resolve_source_type`'s locked vocabulary (max 9 bytes)
