     9	//! # The upstream mechanism (sqlite-vec `=0.1.7`, `sqlite-vec.c`)
    10	//!
    11	//! A vec0 plain-TEXT metadata column stores a 16-byte inline view per row
    12	//! (`VEC0_METADATA_TEXT_VIEW_BUFFER_LENGTH`): a 4-byte length plus the first 12
    13	//! bytes of the value (`VEC0_METADATA_TEXT_VIEW_DATA_LENGTH`). A value LONGER
    14	//! than those 12 bytes additionally gets a row in the `<tbl>_metadatatext<NN>`
    15	//! shadow table.
    16	//!
    17	//! `vec0Update_Delete_ClearMetadata` (`sqlite-vec.c:8888`) deletes that shadow row
    18	//! (`sqlite-vec.c:8934-8952`) and leaves `rc` holding `sqlite3_step`'s
    19	//! `SQLITE_DONE` (101) — it never resets `rc` to `SQLITE_OK`. Its epilogue then
    20	//! returns `rc` verbatim, so a SUCCESSFUL shadow delete is reported to
